\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {F.2}{\ignorespaces Numerical validation of rates in the unselective regime. (a) Reference dephasing rate \(\gamma _{b\uparrow }^{\mathrm  {un}}+\gamma _{c\phi }^{\mathrm  {un}}\) extracted from the procedure in App.~\ref {app:dephasing_numerics} with \(\delta \Phi (t)=0\), compared with the analytical approximation in Eq.~\eqref  {eq:gamma_unselective_approx}. (b) Flux-noise-induced depolarization rate \(\gamma _{b\uparrow }^{1/f,\mathrm  {un}}\) versus noise amplitude \(S_0\). The quadratic scaling in \(S_0\) and agreement with \(\gamma _{b\uparrow }^{1/f,\mathrm  {un}}=\left (\frac  {\partial \omega _b}{\partial \Phi }\right )^2\frac  {S_0^2}{4K}\) (black dashed line) are observed. (c) Cavity decay rate with sweet-spot drive.}}{168}{figure.1.F.2}\protected@file@percent }
